['Here is a simple code snippet that demonstrates how such functionality might be implemented using Java's ExecutorService for asynchronous processing and Future to handle transient errors. Note that this is a simplified example and does not include integration with an external metadata service or handling of malformed file paths or symbolic links, nor does it account for performance optimizations like memory usage optimization, batching, or horizontal scaling.

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class FileProcessor {
    private static final int BATCH_SIZE = 10000;

    public void processFilePaths(List<String> filePaths) throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(5); // or use a cached thread pool for more dynamic scaling
        List<Future<?>> futures = new ArrayList<>();

        long startTime;
        int i = 0;
        Set<String> directories = new HashSet<>();
        for (String filePath : filePaths) {
            if (i % BATCH_SIZE == 0) {
                // batch is full, submit for processing
                futures.add(executor.submit(() ->  processBatch(directories)));

                // reset for next batch
                startTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
                directories.clear();
            }

            try {
                Path path = Paths.get(filePath);
                if (Files.exists(path) && Files.isDirectory(path)) {
                    directories.add(filePath);
                }

                i++;
            } catch (InvalidPathException e) {
                System.out.println("Skipping malformed file path: " + filePath);
            }
        }

        // process any remaining files in last batch
        if (!directories.isEmpty()) {
            futures.add(executor.submit(() -> processBatch(directories)));
        }

        // wait for all tasks to complete
        for (Future<?> future : futures) {
            future.get();
        }

        executor.shutdown();
    }

    private void processBatch(Set<String> directories) {
        long count = directories.size();
        System.out.println("Processed " + count + " unique directories in " + (System.currentTimeMillis() - startTime) + " milliseconds.");

        // insert logic for integration with metadata service here, and handle transient errors
    }
}
```
Please note that this is a very simplistic example and does not account for several considerations mentioned in the problem description such as handling of symbolic links or malformed file paths, integration with an external metadata service, performance optimizations like memory usage optimization, batching, horizontal scaling etc.
