['Here's a basic implementation of your request using C++14 features. This implementation assumes an external "getAttack" function which returns the next attack from the pool of 3 attacks. It uses std::condition_variable, std::mutex and std::chrono for cooldown management, system dependencies handling and resource constraints management. Please note that this is a simplified example, more complete solution would involve additional considerations like error handling, thread-safety etc.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <thread>
#include <mutex>
#include <condition_variable>
#include <chrono>

// Assuming an external function that returns the next attack from a pool of 3 attacks
int getAttack();

std::mutex mtx;
std::condition_variable cv;
bool ready = true;

void executeCombatSequence() {
    int attacks = 0;
    auto nextReleaseTime = std::chrono::system_clock::now();

    while (attacks < 1000) {
        std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lck(mtx);

        // Wait for the cooldown to be over if it hasn't been already.
        cv.wait_until(lck, nextReleaseTime, []{ return ready; });

        int attack = getAttack();
        std::cout << "Selected attack: " << attack << '\n';
        attacks++;

        // Reset the cooldown period for the next attack.
        if(attacks < 1000) {
            ready = false;
            lck.unlock();

            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::seconds(9));

            nextReleaseTime = std::chrono::system_clock::now() + std::chrono::seconds(9);
        }
    }
}
```

This function will execute an attack from the pool of 3 attacks, print it to the console and then wait for a cooldown period of 9 seconds. The cooldown can be interrupted by game events or external systems, which will cause the attack to be repeated immediately when the condition variable is notified that it's ready again.

The function will execute up to 1000 attacks, then stop execution. This limit can easily be changed by changing the `attacks < 1000` comparison in the while loop. If you need to adjust the cooldown period or the total number of possible attacks, this code can be easily adjusted as well.
']

