This implementation also lacks mechanisms for reference counting to avoid premature freeing of shared resources and it doesn't support concurrent access from multiple threads without causing data corruption. Implementing those requires more complex synchronization strategies such as atomic operations or a reference counting system. This would make the code considerably more complicated.
