Remember, C is a low-level language and has no built-in garbage collector. Therefore, we have to manually manage memory, which can be quite error prone if not done carefully. The `free` function will only free the memory allocated by `malloc` or `calloc`, so you should always call it on each pointer that was returned from such a function, and no others.

